  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Positive Jo-1 Antibody</strong>&nbsp;is strongly associated with&nbsp;<strong>idiopathic inflammatory myopathies</strong>, primarily&nbsp;<strong>polymyositis</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>dermatomyositis</strong>, frequently linked with&nbsp;<strong>interstitial lung disease</strong>&nbsp;(fibrosing alveolitis) and features such as polyarthritis and Raynaud&rsquo;s phenomenon.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Jo-1 antibody positivity often precedes clinical myositis onset and serves as an important marker for&nbsp;<strong>anti-synthetase syndrome</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>Negative result</strong>&nbsp;does not exclude idiopathic inflammatory myositis.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Equivocal or weak positive results may require repeat testing or further clinical correlation.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
